IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-interpretation`

-- g6-art15-16-deregistration.l4: Articles 15 and 16 of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014, Deregistration on application by entity, and Deregistration in other cases.
-- Inputs from other groups (PLAN section (c)): IP6 `the entity is a registered charity` (G1); IP8 `the entity meets the charity test` (G2); IP19 `the required steps notices served` (G8).
-- Outputs: IP27 the decisions of the Commissioner under Articles 15(3) and 16 (`Decision of the Commissioner`), IP32 `the basis of deregistration` (`Basis of deregistration`).
-- A discretion is an input: "satisfied", "proportionate", "reasonable time", "grounds relating to the proposals" and "misled" are determinations the caller supplies; none is computed.
-- Dates are DATEs. The day on which the Commissioner acts is a GIVEN, `the day in question`. The effects of a deregistration (Article 17) are in g6-art17-after-deregistration.

§ `Part 4 -- Registration of charities`

§§ `Article 15 -- Deregistration on application by entity`

-- What the entity and the Commissioner do under Articles 15 and 16, value-actor style: the first actor field of each act is its performer.
DECLARE `Act under Article 15 or 16` IS ONE OF
    `apply to the Commissioner to terminate the registration` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `provide the Commissioner with the information or document requested` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `deregister the entity` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `refuse to deregister the entity on grounds relating to the proposals` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `refuse to deregister the entity because paragraph (2) has not been complied with` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `deregister the entity by written notice` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`
    `prescribe by Order a circumstance in which the entity is deregistered` HAS by IS A `Legal actor`

§§§ `Article 15(1) -- a registered charity may apply to deregister`

-- src:430 | (1) An entity that is a registered charity may apply to the Commissioner to terminate the registration of the entity as a charity (to “deregister” the entity).
@ref Article 15(1) (src:430)
@export Whether a registered charity may apply to the Commissioner to terminate its registration (deregister); no such permission arises for an entity that is not a registered charity
GIVEN `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the entity is entered in the general or the restricted section of the register
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 15 or 16`
`Art 15(1) the registered charity may apply to be deregistered` `the entity is a registered charity` MEANS
    IF   `the entity is a registered charity`
    THEN PARTY `a registered charity`
         MAY   `apply to the Commissioner to terminate the registration` `a registered charity`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `Article 15(2) -- the information the Commissioner requests`

-- The duty is that of an entity "applying for deregistration", and covers "any information or document requested by the Commissioner in relation to the entity's proposals for the continuation or winding up
-- of the entity and for the application of any of its property remaining after deregistration": a request about something else gives rise to no duty under this paragraph. No period is stated.
-- src:431 | (2) An entity applying for deregistration must provide the Commissioner with any information or document requested by the Commissioner in relation to the entity’s proposals for the continuation or winding up of the entity and for the application of any of its property remaining after deregistration.
@ref Article 15(2) (src:431)
@export Whether and how an entity applying for deregistration must provide the Commissioner with the information or document the Commissioner requested about its proposals for continuation or winding up and for its remaining property
GIVEN `the entity has applied for deregistration` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the entity has applied under Article 15(1)
      `the Commissioner has requested information or a document about the entity's proposals` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the Commissioner has requested information or a document in relation to the entity's proposals for the continuation or winding up of the entity and for the application of its remaining property
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 15 or 16`
`Art 15(2) the entity must provide the information requested` `the entity has applied for deregistration` `the Commissioner has requested information or a document about the entity's proposals` MEANS
    IF       `the entity has applied for deregistration`
         AND `the Commissioner has requested information or a document about the entity's proposals`
    THEN PARTY `a registered charity`
         MUST  `provide the Commissioner with the information or document requested` `a registered charity`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `Article 15(3) -- the Commissioner must deregister or refuse`

@ref Article 15(3)(a) (src:433)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 15 or 16`
`Art 15(3)(a) the Commissioner must deregister the entity` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST  `deregister the entity` `the Commissioner`
    HENCE FULFILLED

@ref Article 15(3)(b) (src:434)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 15 or 16`
`Art 15(3)(b) the Commissioner must refuse to deregister the entity on grounds relating to the proposals` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST  `refuse to deregister the entity on grounds relating to the proposals` `the Commissioner`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- (3)(a) or (b), when the entity complies: the Commissioner does one of the two, so the duties are alternatives (ROR), each unguarded. The refusal is available only "on grounds relating to the proposals".
@ref Article 15(3) (src:432-434)
GIVEN `the grounds for refusing relate to the proposals mentioned in paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 15 or 16`
`Art 15(3) the duty of the Commissioner where the entity has complied` `the grounds for refusing relate to the proposals mentioned in paragraph (2)` MEANS
    IF   `the grounds for refusing relate to the proposals mentioned in paragraph (2)`
    THEN `Art 15(3)(a) the Commissioner must deregister the entity`
         ROR `Art 15(3)(b) the Commissioner must refuse to deregister the entity on grounds relating to the proposals`
    ELSE `Art 15(3)(a) the Commissioner must deregister the entity`

-- F6.1: the paragraph says what the Commissioner must do "if the entity complies with paragraph (2)" and says nothing of the case where it does not.
-- Reading taken: no duty arises under paragraph (3); the application stays where it is. The others: the Commissioner may refuse (B), must refuse (C), or the Law states no rule, and the question has no answer (D).
@ref Article 15(3) (F6.1) (src:432)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 15 or 16`
`F6.1 reading B: the Commissioner may refuse to deregister` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MAY   `refuse to deregister the entity because paragraph (2) has not been complied with` `the Commissioner`
    HENCE FULFILLED

@ref Article 15(3) (F6.1) (src:432)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 15 or 16`
`F6.1 reading C: the Commissioner must refuse to deregister` MEANS
    PARTY `the Commissioner`
    MUST  `refuse to deregister the entity because paragraph (2) has not been complied with` `the Commissioner`
    HENCE FULFILLED

@ref Article 15(3) (src:432)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 15 or 16`
`F6.1 reading D: the Law states no rule for an application where paragraph (2) has not been complied with` MEANS
    REFUSE "Article 15(3) states what the Commissioner must do if the entity complies with paragraph (2), and the Law states no rule for the case where it does not"

@ref Article 15(2) and (3) (F6.1) (src:431-432)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 15 or 16`
`Art 15(3) where the entity has not complied with paragraph (2)` interp MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `what follows where the entity has not complied with Article 15(2)`
    WHEN `no duty arises under Article 15(3)` THEN FULFILLED
    WHEN `the Commissioner may refuse to deregister` THEN `F6.1 reading B: the Commissioner may refuse to deregister`
    WHEN `the Commissioner must refuse to deregister` THEN `F6.1 reading C: the Commissioner must refuse to deregister`
    WHEN `the Law states no rule for that case` THEN `F6.1 reading D: the Law states no rule for an application where paragraph (2) has not been complied with`

-- src:432 | (3) If the entity complies with paragraph (2) the Commissioner must –
-- src:433 | (a) deregister the entity; or
-- src:434 | (b) refuse to deregister the entity on grounds relating to the proposals mentioned in paragraph (2).
@ref Article 15(3) (src:432-434)
@export Whether and how the Commissioner must deregister an entity that has applied, or refuse on grounds relating to its proposals, if the entity has complied with Article 15(2); where it has not, the result depends on the reading given (by default no duty arises)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
        @desc The readings of the open points of Articles 15 to 20; here F6.1 (what follows where the entity has not complied with paragraph (2))
      `the entity has applied for deregistration` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the entity has applied under Article 15(1)
      `the entity has complied with Article 15(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the entity has provided all the information and documents the Commissioner requested about its proposals
      `the grounds for refusing relate to the proposals mentioned in paragraph (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc The Commissioner's determination whether there are grounds, relating to the entity's proposals, for refusing to deregister
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 15 or 16`
`Art 15(3) the Commissioner must deregister or refuse` interp `the entity has applied for deregistration` `the entity has complied with Article 15(2)` `the grounds for refusing relate to the proposals mentioned in paragraph (2)` MEANS
    IF   NOT `the entity has applied for deregistration`
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE IF   `the entity has complied with Article 15(2)`
         THEN `Art 15(3) the duty of the Commissioner where the entity has complied` `the grounds for refusing relate to the proposals mentioned in paragraph (2)`
         ELSE `Art 15(3) where the entity has not complied with paragraph (2)` interp

-- IP27: the decision of the Commissioner under Article 15(3) is the single decision "whether to deregister on application": the outcome is that the Commissioner does what the entity sought (deregisters) or refuses.
-- src:432 | (3) If the entity complies with paragraph (2) the Commissioner must –
-- src:433 | (a) deregister the entity; or
-- src:434 | (b) refuse to deregister the entity on grounds relating to the proposals mentioned in paragraph (2).
@ref Article 15(3) (src:432-434)
@export The decision of the Commissioner under Article 15(3), as a subject and an outcome (IP27): deregistering is doing what was sought, refusing is refusing
GIVEN `the Commissioner deregisters the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc TRUE if the Commissioner deregisters the entity under Article 15(3)(a); FALSE if the Commissioner refuses under (3)(b)
GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`Art 15(3) the decision of the Commissioner` `the Commissioner deregisters the entity` MEANS
    `Decision of the Commissioner` WITH
        subject IS `whether to deregister a charity on its own application, Article 15(3)`
        outcome IS IF   `the Commissioner deregisters the entity`
                    THEN `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`
                    ELSE `the Commissioner refuses`

§§ `Article 16 -- Deregistration in other cases`

-- The notice that must come first (Article 16(1)): "written notice specifying reasons and inviting objections within a reasonable time specified in the notice". The three formal parts are facts; the time and its
-- reasonableness are the notice's and a determination.
DECLARE `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)` HAS
    `given on` IS A DATE
        @desc The day the Commissioner gave the entity the notice
    `the last day for objections` IS A DATE
        @desc The last day of the time specified in the notice within which objections are invited
    `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the notice is in writing
    `specifies reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the notice specifies reasons
    `invites objections within a time it specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the notice invites objections within a time specified in it
    `the time specified is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc A determination: whether the time the notice specifies for objections is a reasonable time

-- What else the caller knows about the grounds of Article 16(1) and the Commissioner's satisfaction.
DECLARE `Facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)` HAS
    `the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity, by the entity or by any other person and whether intentionally or otherwise
    `a circumstance prescribed by Order under Article 16(1)(d) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether any other circumstance the Minister has prescribed by Order applies
    `the Commissioner is satisfied that it is proportionate to deregister on a ground` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc The Commissioner's satisfaction, after the preliminary notice, that it is proportionate to deregister on one of the grounds

§§§ `Article 16(1) -- deregistration by written notice, after a preliminary notice`

-- The four grounds. A ground exists when its condition holds; the Commissioner must also be satisfied that it is proportionate to deregister on it (a determination).
-- src:437 | (a) the entity no longer meets the charity test;
@ref Article 16(1)(a) (src:437)
@export Whether the ground of Article 16(1)(a) exists: the entity no longer meets the charity test
GIVEN `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the entity meets the charity test of Article 5 (IP8)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 16(1)(a) the entity no longer meets the charity test` `the entity meets the charity test` MEANS
    NOT `the entity meets the charity test`

-- src:438 | (b) the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity, whether by the entity or by any other person and whether intentionally or otherwise;
@ref Article 16(1)(b) (src:438)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 16(1)(b) the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity` facts MEANS
    facts's `the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity`

-- F6.19: "the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice". A notice served on the charity that has not been complied with counts as failed to comply once the time the notice names has ended
-- without the steps taken (the reading taken; a notice that names no time can be failed as soon as the steps have not been taken). The other reading counts any notice whose steps have not yet been taken.
-- A governor's notice is not the entity's.
@ref Article 16(1)(c) (F6.19) (src:439)
GIVEN `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.19 reading A: the notice has not been complied with once the time it names has ended without the steps taken` `the required steps notices served` day MEANS
    any (GIVEN notice YIELD
                notice's `served on` EQUALS `the registered charity`
            AND NOT notice's `has been complied with`
            AND CONSIDER notice's `steps to be taken by`
                WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
                WHEN JUST last THEN last LESS THAN day)
        `the required steps notices served`

@ref Article 16(1)(c) (F6.19) (src:439)
GIVEN `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.19 reading B: the notice has not been complied with whenever the steps have not yet been taken` `the required steps notices served` MEANS
    any (GIVEN notice YIELD
                notice's `served on` EQUALS `the registered charity`
            AND NOT notice's `has been complied with`)
        `the required steps notices served`

-- src:439 | (c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice; or
@ref Article 16(1)(c) (src:439)
@export Whether the ground of Article 16(1)(c) exists: the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice served on it, on the reading given of when a notice has not been complied with
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
        @desc The readings of the open points of Articles 15 to 20; here F6.19 (when the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice)
      `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
        @desc The required steps notices served on the charity or on its governors (IP19)
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
        @desc The day on which the Commissioner acts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` interp `the required steps notices served` `the day in question` MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `when the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice`
    WHEN `the notice has not been complied with once the time it names has ended without the steps taken`
        THEN `F6.19 reading A: the notice has not been complied with once the time it names has ended without the steps taken` `the required steps notices served` `the day in question`
    WHEN `the notice has not been complied with whenever the steps have not yet been taken`
        THEN `F6.19 reading B: the notice has not been complied with whenever the steps have not yet been taken` `the required steps notices served`

-- src:440 | (d) any other circumstance prescribed by the Minister by Order applies.
@ref Article 16(1)(d) (src:440)
GIVEN facts IS A `Facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 16(1)(d) a circumstance prescribed by the Minister by Order applies` facts MEANS
    facts's `a circumstance prescribed by Order under Article 16(1)(d) applies`

-- The power behind (d): the Minister may prescribe a circumstance by Order. What the Order says is an input (the caller's `a circumstance prescribed by Order under Article 16(1)(d) applies`).
-- src:440 | (d) any other circumstance prescribed by the Minister by Order applies.
@ref Article 16(1)(d) (src:440)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 15 or 16`
`Art 16(1)(d) the Minister may prescribe a circumstance of deregistration by Order` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY   `prescribe by Order a circumstance in which the entity is deregistered` `the Minister`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- Some ground exists: (a), (b), (c) or (d).
-- src:436 | (1) The Commissioner may, by written notice to an entity that is registered as a charity, deregister the entity if satisfied, after giving the entity written notice specifying reasons and inviting objections within a reasonable time specified in the notice, that it is proportionate to do so on the ground that –
-- src:437 | (a) the entity no longer meets the charity test;
-- src:438 | (b) the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity, whether by the entity or by any other person and whether intentionally or otherwise;
-- src:439 | (c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice; or
-- src:440 | (d) any other circumstance prescribed by the Minister by Order applies.
@ref Article 16(1) (src:436-440)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
      facts IS A `Facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 16(1) a ground of Article 16(1) exists` interp `the entity meets the charity test` `the required steps notices served` facts `the day in question` MEANS
        "the Commissioner ... that it is proportionate to do so on the ground that –"
    ..  "(a)" ... `Art 16(1)(a) the entity no longer meets the charity test` `the entity meets the charity test`
    ..  "(b)" ... `Art 16(1)(b) the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity` facts
    ..  "(c)" ... `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` interp `the required steps notices served` `the day in question`
    OR  "(d)" ... `Art 16(1)(d) a circumstance prescribed by the Minister by Order applies` facts

-- F6.13: "inviting objections within a reasonable time specified in the notice". The notice must invite objections within a time it specifies, and that time must be a reasonable one: reading taken, a notice
-- whose time is not reasonable is not the notice paragraph (1) requires, so the deregistration is not authorised. The other reading: any time specified suffices.
@ref Article 16(1) (src:436)
GIVEN notice IS A `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the preliminary notice has its three formal parts` notice MEANS
        notice's `in writing`
    AND notice's `specifies reasons`
    AND notice's `invites objections within a time it specifies`

@ref Article 16(1) (F6.13) (src:436)
GIVEN notice IS A `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.13 reading A: the time specified must be reasonable or the deregistration is not authorised` notice MEANS
        `the preliminary notice has its three formal parts` notice
    AND notice's `the time specified is reasonable`

@ref Article 16(1) (F6.13) (src:436)
GIVEN notice IS A `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.13 reading B: any time specified suffices` notice MEANS
    `the preliminary notice has its three formal parts` notice

@ref Article 16(1) (F6.13) (src:436)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      notice IS A `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 16(1) the preliminary notice is the notice the paragraph requires` interp notice MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `whether the time for objections must be reasonable`
    WHEN `the time specified must be reasonable or the deregistration is not authorised`
        THEN `F6.13 reading A: the time specified must be reasonable or the deregistration is not authorised` notice
    WHEN `any time specified suffices`
        THEN `F6.13 reading B: any time specified suffices` notice

-- F6.17: when the Commissioner may deregister after giving the preliminary notice. The words are "if satisfied, after giving the entity written notice ... inviting objections within a reasonable time specified in the notice":
-- the satisfaction comes after the notice is given. Reading taken: the invitation would be empty if the Commissioner could deregister before the time ran out, so only after the last day for objections.
-- The day of the notice itself is inside the "after giving" on the first reading (a date has no hour: the notice may precede the deregistration within the day).
@ref Article 16(1) (F6.17) (src:436)
GIVEN notice IS A `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.17 reading A: the Commissioner may deregister at any time after the notice is given` notice day MEANS
    notice's `given on` AT MOST day

@ref Article 16(1) (F6.17) (src:436)
GIVEN notice IS A `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.17 reading B: the Commissioner may deregister only after the last day for objections` notice day MEANS
    notice's `the last day for objections` LESS THAN day

@ref Article 16(1) (F6.17) (src:436)
GIVEN notice IS A `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.17 reading C: the Commissioner may deregister only on or after the last day for objections` notice day MEANS
    notice's `the last day for objections` AT MOST day

@ref Article 16(1) (F6.17) (src:436)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      notice IS A `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 16(1) the time for objections allows deregistration on the day` interp notice day MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `when the Commissioner may deregister after giving the preliminary notice`
    WHEN `the Commissioner may deregister at any time after the notice is given`
        THEN `F6.17 reading A: the Commissioner may deregister at any time after the notice is given` notice day
    WHEN `the Commissioner may deregister only after the last day for objections`
        THEN `F6.17 reading B: the Commissioner may deregister only after the last day for objections` notice day
    WHEN `the Commissioner may deregister only on or after the last day for objections`
        THEN `F6.17 reading C: the Commissioner may deregister only on or after the last day for objections` notice day

-- The preliminary notice has been given, is the notice the paragraph requires, and the Commissioner may deregister on the day. No notice at all: none of it.
@ref Article 16(1) (src:436)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      notice IS A MAYBE `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 16(1) the procedure of the preliminary notice has been followed by the day` interp notice day MEANS
    CONSIDER notice
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST given THEN
            `Art 16(1) the preliminary notice is the notice the paragraph requires` interp given
        AND `Art 16(1) the time for objections allows deregistration on the day` interp given day

-- src:436 | (1) The Commissioner may, by written notice to an entity that is registered as a charity, deregister the entity if satisfied, after giving the entity written notice specifying reasons and inviting objections within a reasonable time specified in the notice, that it is proportionate to do so on the ground that –
@ref Article 16(1) (src:436)
@export Whether and how the Commissioner may, by written notice, deregister an entity that is registered as a charity: a ground exists, a preliminary notice giving reasons and inviting objections has been given and has run its time, and the Commissioner is satisfied that deregistering is proportionate; the answer is a permission (MAY) of the Commissioner, or nothing
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
        @desc The readings of the open points of Articles 15 to 20; here F6.13 (whether the time for objections must be reasonable), F6.17 (when deregistration may follow the preliminary notice) and F6.19 (when a required steps notice has not been complied with)
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the entity is entered in the general or the restricted section of the register
      `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the entity meets the charity test of Article 5 (IP8)
      `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
        @desc The required steps notices served on the charity or on its governors (IP19)
      facts IS A `Facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)`
        @desc The facts about the grounds and the Commissioner's satisfaction
      notice IS A MAYBE `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)`
        @desc The preliminary notice; NOTHING if none has been given
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
        @desc The day on which the Commissioner would deregister
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 15 or 16`
`Art 16(1) the Commissioner may deregister the entity` interp `the entity is a registered charity` `the entity meets the charity test` `the required steps notices served` facts notice `the day in question` MEANS
    IF       `the entity is a registered charity`
         AND `Art 16(1) a ground of Article 16(1) exists` interp `the entity meets the charity test` `the required steps notices served` facts `the day in question`
         AND facts's `the Commissioner is satisfied that it is proportionate to deregister on a ground`
         AND `Art 16(1) the procedure of the preliminary notice has been followed by the day` interp notice `the day in question`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY   `deregister the entity by written notice` `the Commissioner`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `Article 16(2) -- the Commissioner must deregister an entity that no longer exists`

-- F6.2: Article 16(1) is a power, after a preliminary notice; Article 16(2) is a duty, "if the Commissioner is satisfied that an entity ... no longer exists". Reading taken: the duty arises on the satisfaction,
-- with no preliminary notice (a notice inviting objections from an entity that no longer exists would be futile, and the paragraph names the persons to whom the deregistering notice goes). The other reading
-- keeps the procedure of paragraph (1): the duty arises only once the preliminary notice has been given and has run its time.
@ref Article 16(1) and (2) (F6.2) (src:436) (src:441)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      notice IS A MAYBE `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F6.2 the procedure of Article 16(1) that Article 16(2) requires` interp notice day MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `how Article 16(2) relates to the procedure of Article 16(1)`
    WHEN `Article 16(2) governs alone and the duty arises on satisfaction with no prior notice` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Article 16(2) follows the procedure of Article 16(1) and the duty arises only after the prior notice has run its time`
        THEN `Art 16(1) the procedure of the preliminary notice has been followed by the day` interp notice day

-- src:441 | (2) If the Commissioner is satisfied that an entity that is registered as a charity no longer exists, the Commissioner must, by written notice to any person purporting to be a governor of the entity or to be responsible for the winding up of the affairs of the entity, deregister the entity.
@ref Article 16(2) (src:441)
@export Whether and how the Commissioner must, by written notice to a person purporting to be a governor or responsible for winding up, deregister an entity that is registered as a charity and that the Commissioner is satisfied no longer exists
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
        @desc The readings of the open points of Articles 15 to 20; here F6.2 (how Article 16(2) relates to the procedure of Article 16(1)), F6.13 and F6.17
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc Whether the entity is entered in the general or the restricted section of the register
      `the Commissioner is satisfied that the entity no longer exists` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc The Commissioner's satisfaction that the entity no longer exists
      notice IS A MAYBE `Preliminary notice of Article 16(1)`
        @desc The preliminary notice of Article 16(1), if one was given (read only under the reading that keeps that procedure)
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
        @desc The day on which the Commissioner would deregister
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 15 or 16`
`Art 16(2) the Commissioner must deregister the entity that no longer exists` interp `the entity is a registered charity` `the Commissioner is satisfied that the entity no longer exists` notice `the day in question` MEANS
    IF       `the entity is a registered charity`
         AND `the Commissioner is satisfied that the entity no longer exists`
         AND `F6.2 the procedure of Article 16(1) that Article 16(2) requires` interp notice `the day in question`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MUST  `deregister the entity by written notice` `the Commissioner`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- IP27: the decision of the Commissioner under Article 16, "whether to deregister" in other cases: the outcome is deregistering (what was proposed) or declining to.
-- src:436 | (1) The Commissioner may, by written notice to an entity that is registered as a charity, deregister the entity if satisfied, after giving the entity written notice specifying reasons and inviting objections within a reasonable time specified in the notice, that it is proportionate to do so on the ground that –
-- src:437 | (a) the entity no longer meets the charity test;
-- src:438 | (b) the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity, whether by the entity or by any other person and whether intentionally or otherwise;
-- src:439 | (c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice; or
-- src:440 | (d) any other circumstance prescribed by the Minister by Order applies.
-- src:441 | (2) If the Commissioner is satisfied that an entity that is registered as a charity no longer exists, the Commissioner must, by written notice to any person purporting to be a governor of the entity or to be responsible for the winding up of the affairs of the entity, deregister the entity.
@ref Article 16(1) and (2) (src:436) (src:441)
@export The decision of the Commissioner under Article 16, as a subject and an outcome (IP27): deregistering is doing what was proposed, not deregistering is refusing
GIVEN `the Commissioner deregisters the entity` IS A BOOLEAN
        @desc TRUE if the Commissioner deregisters the entity under Article 16(1) or (2); FALSE if the Commissioner decides not to
GIVETH A `Decision of the Commissioner`
`Art 16 the decision of the Commissioner` `the Commissioner deregisters the entity` MEANS
    `Decision of the Commissioner` WITH
        subject IS `whether to deregister a charity in other cases, Article 16`
        outcome IS IF   `the Commissioner deregisters the entity`
                    THEN `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`
                    ELSE `the Commissioner refuses`

§§§ `Articles 15 and 16 -- why the entity was deregistered`

-- How the Commissioner came to deregister, from which the basis of the deregistration follows (IP32, read by G3 for the historic section and by G8 for the right of appeal, which lies against a deregistration).
DECLARE `Route by which the Commissioner deregistered the entity` IS ONE OF
    `on the entity's own application under Article 15(3)(a)`
    `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the entity no longer meets the charity test`
    `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity`
    `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice`
    `by written notice under Article 16(1) on a circumstance prescribed by Order`
    `by written notice under Article 16(2) because the entity no longer exists`

-- src:433 | (a) deregister the entity; or
-- src:437 | (a) the entity no longer meets the charity test;
-- src:438 | (b) the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity, whether by the entity or by any other person and whether intentionally or otherwise;
-- src:439 | (c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice; or
-- src:440 | (d) any other circumstance prescribed by the Minister by Order applies.
-- src:441 | (2) If the Commissioner is satisfied that an entity that is registered as a charity no longer exists, the Commissioner must, by written notice to any person purporting to be a governor of the entity or to be responsible for the winding up of the affairs of the entity, deregister the entity.
@ref Articles 15(3)(a) and 16 (src:433) (src:437-441)
@export Why an entity was deregistered, as the basis of deregistration (IP32): on its own application, or on one of the four grounds of Article 16(1), or because it no longer exists
GIVEN route IS A `Route by which the Commissioner deregistered the entity`
        @desc How the Commissioner deregistered the entity
GIVETH A `Basis of deregistration`
`Art 16 the basis of deregistration` route MEANS
    CONSIDER route
    WHEN `on the entity's own application under Article 15(3)(a)` THEN `on the entity's own application under Article 15`
    WHEN `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the entity no longer meets the charity test` THEN `the entity no longer meets the charity test`
    WHEN `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity` THEN `the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity`
    WHEN `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` THEN `the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice`
    WHEN `by written notice under Article 16(1) on a circumstance prescribed by Order` THEN `a circumstance prescribed by Order under Article 16(1)(d)`
    WHEN `by written notice under Article 16(2) because the entity no longer exists` THEN `the entity no longer exists`

-- Whether the ground the Commissioner relied on exists on the facts: for a deregistration under Article 16(1) on one of the four grounds, that ground; for the others, nothing further is asked.
@ref Article 16(1) and (2) (src:437-441)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 15 to 20`
      route IS A `Route by which the Commissioner deregistered the entity`
      `the entity meets the charity test` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the required steps notices served` IS A LIST OF `Required steps notice`
      facts IS A `Facts about the grounds of Article 16(1)`
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 16(1) the ground relied on exists` interp route `the entity meets the charity test` `the required steps notices served` facts `the day in question` MEANS
    CONSIDER route
    WHEN `on the entity's own application under Article 15(3)(a)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the entity no longer meets the charity test`
        THEN `Art 16(1)(a) the entity no longer meets the charity test` `the entity meets the charity test`
    WHEN `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity`
        THEN `Art 16(1)(b) the Commissioner was misled into registering the entity` facts
    WHEN `by written notice under Article 16(1) on the ground that the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice`
        THEN `Art 16(1)(c) the entity has failed to comply with a required steps notice` interp `the required steps notices served` `the day in question`
    WHEN `by written notice under Article 16(1) on a circumstance prescribed by Order`
        THEN `Art 16(1)(d) a circumstance prescribed by the Minister by Order applies` facts
    WHEN `by written notice under Article 16(2) because the entity no longer exists` THEN TRUE
